retabbed
========
tabbed 0.9 with the window grouping, mouse feedback, shortcuts, and fixes
from jOS. the executable and X11 class remain tabbed for compatibility.

build and install
-----------------
requires a c compiler, make, and the Xlib, Xft, and fontconfig headers and
libraries. the checks also need address/undefined sanitizers and a linker
supporting --wrap.

    make
    make check
    make install

the default prefix is /usr/local. override it with make PREFIX=/your/path
or use DESTDIR for a staged installation. edit config.def.h for persistent
configuration; a newer config.def.h overwrites config.h on the next build.

usage
-----
run an application with XEmbed support:

    tabbed surf -e
    tabbed xterm -into

group existing top-level X11 windows (replace these example ids):

    tabbed -c -G 0x100001 -G 0x200001

left-click selects a tab, middle-click closes it, and the wheel changes
tabs. grouped tabs highlight on hover. ctrl+tab / ctrl+shift+tab cycle
tabs; ctrl+F4 or ctrl+shift+w closes the selected tab. opening new tabs
with ctrl+shift+t requires ordinary command-based mode.

closing a grouped container requests closure of its selected application,
including the final tab. detaching a tab returns it to the desktop. jOS's
dwm supplies the group/detach shortcuts; this standalone repo contains
the tabbed side of that integration.

see tabbed(1) for all options and PATCHES.md for every local difference
from the supplied tabbed 0.9 baseline, title behavior, integration details,
and the limits of the automated checks. the original license is in LICENSE.
